om/vi/Ok-5lWGBQr8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T04:52:49-08:00","id":1028503,"title":"","content":"<i>Ravenous</i>. Good beast vs. bad beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T04:46:18-08:00","id":1028967,"title":"","content":"Of the horror classics, I feel Candyman has the right vibe for Beast. A good example of the Infestation Atavism, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T00:57:41-08:00","id":1035655,"title":"","content":"I watched <i>Babadook</i> and still I do not feel I get it as <b>Beast</b> inspiration. I understand it's story of Amelia Devouring and with her son Samuel starting to react as Hero - but what Family would be Babadook itself? What would it be Hunger? I suspect that Babadook is Eshmaki - as he is Horror of Things in Darkness - but I still do not know what was his 'motivation' in movie. Is he there as to confront Amelia's loss of her husband?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T01:03:05-08:00","id":1035656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1027789-btp-movies?p=1035655#post1035655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I watched <i>Babadook</i> and still I do not feel I get it as <b>Beast</b> inspiration. I understand it's story of Amelia Devouring and with her son Samuel starting to react as Hero - but what Family would be Babadook itself? What would it be Hunger? I suspect that Babadook is Eshmaki - as he is Horror of Things in Darkness - but I still do not know what was his 'motivation' in movie. Is he there as to confront Amelia's loss of her husband?</div> </div> </div> </div>From how i see it.. the Babadok has a hunger for Ruin. He wants to see her fail at a normal family life... and Destroy her own humanity (her Son)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T01:17:52-08:00","id":1035658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1027789-btp-movies?p=1035656#post1035656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From how i see it.. the Babadok has a hunger for Ruin. He wants to see her fail at a normal family life... and Destroy her own humanity (her Son)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, this makes perfect sense! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:44:23-08:00","id":1043201,"title":"","content":"Not a movie, but there's Marvel/Netflix's Daredevil.<br /> <br /> Show is centered around an Eshmaki Nemesis (Daredevil/Matt Murdock), trying to reconcile his own desire for justice while attempting to deny his Horror that just enjoys beating up people. The external conflict about an Anakim Tyrant (Kingpin/Wilson Fisk), trying to make himself the Apex of New York, starting with Hell's Kitchen, and by trying to bring all the other crime families under his control. With the two naturally clashing with each other when their Hungers have a...conflict of interest. <br /> <br /> The second season being about a former lover (Elektra) who also happened to be of the same Family and Hunger, trying to go all in with indulging in his Hunger, aka actually killing his targets.<br /> <br /> ...also when I was first watching the show, it did occur to me that Beast vs Beast conflicts was actually a very fascinating conflict to explore.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:12:55-08:00","id":1043221,"title":"","content":"Nightmare on Elm Street! Freddy is an urban legend that gets all up inside your dreams and terrorizes you to death. I can't help but think of Beasts as little Krueggies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"